# Copy this file to `.env` (same directory) and paste your real Supabase
# SESSION-POOLER connection string. `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Get the string from the Supabase dashboard: Connect -> Session pooler.
# Slot your saved database password in place of [YOUR-PASSWORD].
# Port is 5432 for the session pooler (not 6543, which is the transaction pooler).
#
# THE SESSION POOLER IS NOW LOAD-BEARING, NOT A PREFERENCE (P5/S4b). The worker waits for jobs with
# Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY, and a LISTEN registration does not survive the TRANSACTION pooler, which
# hands the connection back after every statement. Moving to 6543 would not error — the worker would
# simply never be woken, and would fall back to its 60s safety-net poll silently. If that move is
# ever wanted, change the wait strategy in `data/serve/worker_loop.py` first.
#
# If Postgres rejects the connection over SSL, append: ?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
